Accelerometer (`/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:device0`, Bosch BMA222E, chip ID 0xf8):

```text
in_accel_x_raw = 4
in_accel_y_raw = -8
in_accel_z_raw = 252
```

The touch controller is on BLSP1 QUP5 (`0x78b9000`, GPIO 18/19), not QUP3 as
the first reading of the stock QRD DTS suggested. The stock DTS itself has
both an MStar and a FocalTech node on QUP5; the FT6436 answers as `EP0110M09`.

Not enabled:

* display: stock uses MDP3 (`qcom,mdss_mdp3`) + RM68191 QHD DSI; mainline
  DRM has no MDP3 driver.
* audio/mic: stock uses the internal "tombak" codec + PM8909 WCD analog block
  at SPMI 0xf000; the MSM8909 LPASS/tombak path is not described in mainline.
* ALS/proximity: Epticore EM3071x at 0x24 on QUP1, no mainline driver.

ALS (Epticore EM3071x at 0x24 on QUP1):

```text
iio:device1 em3071x
in_illuminance_raw   = 1
in_illuminance_input = 10
```

The chip ID register returns 0x31 and the ALS count is split over registers
9/10; it only answers SMBus word reads, which is why the first byte-read probe
returned EIO.

Display (simple-framebuffer at LK's 0x83300000, PMIC LPG backlight):

```text
[drm] Initialized simpledrm 1.0.0 for 83300000.framebuffer on minor 0
simple-framebuffer 83300000.framebuffer: [drm] fb0: simpledrmdrmfb frame buffer device
gkiw: framebuffer test pattern drawn
backlight brightness = 255
```

The initial 0x83201000 guess was zero; scanning the stock splash region showed
LK's framebuffer at 0x83300000 (opaque black/gray pixels).  The initramfs fills
`/dev/fb0` with colour bars so the panel visibly shows the framebuffer.

MDP3 DRM/KMS driver (takes over LK's 720x1280 RGB888 scanout):

```text
[drm] Initialized mdp3 1.0.0 for 1a00000.display-controller on minor 0
mdp3-drm 1a00000.display-controller: [drm] fb0: mdp3drmfb frame buffer device
MDP3 primary DMA source = 0x98100000 (CMA buffer)
MDP3 size               = 0x050002d0 (720x1280)
MDP3 stride             = 0x00000870 (2160 = 720 * 3, RGB888)
gkiw: framebuffer test pattern drawn
```

The bootloader-left pipeline is reused; page flips are writes to the primary
DMA address and the fbcon renders on the panel.
